\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Aligned post-centering burst experiment. Continuous-phase Callisto uses the fixed moderate PI coordinates and their full-Fuzzy calibration. Both controllers have their own clean counterfactual. Desired latency on one directed channel changes from 20 to 40 during $[2\times 10^6,2.1\times 10^6)$. Frequency histories use held corrections; buffer overview samples are for display, while reported buffer statistics come from the complete reconstructed event stream.}}{16}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eval_burst_overview}{{1}{16}{Aligned post-centering burst experiment. Continuous-phase Callisto uses the fixed moderate PI coordinates and their full-Fuzzy calibration. Both controllers have their own clean counterfactual. Desired latency on one directed channel changes from 20 to 40 during $[2\times 10^6,2.1\times 10^6)$. Frequency histories use held corrections; buffer overview samples are for display, while reported buffer statistics come from the complete reconstructed event stream}{figure.caption.14}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Nonlinear mechanism diagnostics reusing the four M2 runs. The panels show the exact central residual $F-F_0$, common-frequency memory accounting, command activity and complete early buffer events. The hatched $F_0$ activity bar is a replay on Fuzzy's measured inputs, not a third closed-loop experiment. The residual surface is multiplied by negative $K_u$ in the controller. The memory panel uses $[3.7\times 10^6,4\times 10^6)$; activity uses the main disturbance window. First peak attainment precedes the first changed command, but the peak can be revisited after feedback begins.}}{17}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eval_mechanism}{{2}{17}{Nonlinear mechanism diagnostics reusing the four M2 runs. The panels show the exact central residual $F-F_0$, common-frequency memory accounting, command activity and complete early buffer events. The hatched $F_0$ activity bar is a replay on Fuzzy's measured inputs, not a third closed-loop experiment. The residual surface is multiplied by negative $K_u$ in the controller. The memory panel uses $[3.7\times 10^6,4\times 10^6)$; activity uses the main disturbance window. First peak attainment precedes the first changed command, but the peak can be revisited after feedback begins}{figure.caption.15}{}}
